# uv.lock: foundry-cip is a published library, not a Railway app — requirements-dev.txt
# is the single committed lockfile (FND-S13 library-shape). Do not commit uv.lock.
uv.lock

# Agent scratch zone (JOS-R20) - never commit
.scratchpad/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC. Nothing below may ever be committed here.
#
# WHY THESE RULES ARE TREE-SHAPED, NOT PATH-SHAPED. They replace two narrow
# per-path rules that were written for exactly this risk and still failed: new
# working directories appeared beside the denied ones and were not covered. A
# hand-maintained path list cannot keep up with agents that create their own
# directories. Deny the tree. Do not narrow these rules back into paths.
#
# Build-surface working material (JOS-C47) does not belong in a public repo at
# all. Keep it in a private venture repo.
WORKBENCH/

# Tenant manifests enumerate live client rosters and per-tenant data. They are
# auto-generated by scripts/generate_tenant_manifest.py -- regenerate locally,
# never commit. The one exemption below is a registered governed object in
# docs/_registry.yaml (CIP-DIAG-102) holding schema and row-count diagnostics
# only; removing it requires a registry edit first.
docs/tenants/*
!docs/tenants/dec814db-722a-4730-8e60-51afc4a5dad9/
